#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimize job run time"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Minimize job run time {#minimize-job-run-time}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are several ways you can limit the amount of time spent processing and"
" running a job:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run only as many shots as you need: A job's QPU consumption (and therefore, "
"its cost) scales with the number of shots. Therefore, you can manage your "
"cost by running only as many shots as you need. For Estimator jobs, lower "
"precision typically requires more shots and therefore a longer execution "
"time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set limits on execution time:  You can limit how long each job, batch, or "
"session runs.  For details, see [Maximum execution time for Qiskit Runtime "
"workloads](max-execution-time).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use only the necessary settings for error suppression and error mitigation, "
"because higher values can cause your jobs to run longer. See [Introduction "
"to options](/guides/runtime-options-overview), [Configure error "
"suppression](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques), and "
"[Configure error mitigation](error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) "
"for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- If you are running multiple jobs that contain the same (likely parameterized) circuits and are using an error mitigation method that requires noise models, such as PEA and PEC, consider using `NoiseLearner`. With this helper program, you can learn the noise model of a circuit once and reuse the model in subsequent Estimator queries. Note that a noise model becomes stale after a certain time, so this is only practical if there is no long delay between jobs (for example, within a session). See [Noise learning helper\n"
"](/guides/noise-learning) for more details.\n"
msgstr ""

